        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add publisher follow graph API",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Implements the first publisher-scoped follow graph slice: persistent private follow rows, idempotent follow/unfollow, notification preference state, audit events, and current-user follow listing.\n- Adds the API-token HTTP surface at `/api/v1/publisher-follows` for GET/POST/DELETE plus the `clawhub-schema` route constant and generated Convex API typing.\n- Keeps the RFC boundary intact: following is only discovery/notification preference, not official status, review, scan, install authority, or local approval. Notification fanout and profile/search UX remain follow-up PRs.\n- Keeps `specs/follow-graph-notifications.md` as the design note for the broader track.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- `git diff --cached --check`\n- `npx --yes oxfmt --check convex/lib/retentionPolicy.ts convex/httpApiV1.handlers.test.ts convex/publisherFollows.ts convex/publisherFollows.test.ts convex/httpApiV1/publisherFollowsV1.ts convex/http.ts convex/httpApiV1.ts convex/schema.ts packages/schema/src/routes.ts packages/schema/dist/routes.js packages/schema/dist/routes.d.ts convex/_generated/api.d.ts`\n- `codex review --uncommitted` clean after fixing accepted findings around stale follow-list rows, malformed JSON bodies, and table retention policy\n- `npx vitest run convex/publisherFollows.test.ts convex/httpApiV1.handlers.test.ts` could not run locally because this Windows checkout has no `node_modules`; the repo config imports `vitest/config`, so `npx` alone cannot satisfy it. CI should run the exact tests with installed dependencies.",
